--
A type annotation is documentation, not a runtime coercion: `x: int =
<tagged-union value>` keeps the value's runtime tag rather than reading
__int_val unconditionally. After to_str() makes c.value a str, x retains
the str tag, so isinstance(x, int) is False and the assertion fails.
Previously cbmc-py force-unwrapped to int and verified SUCCESSFUL (the
differential unsoundness witness B). Now detected; promoted to CORE.
